n":null,"multipleYAxes":{"additional":[],"showMultiplePanels":false,"base":{"horizontalLines":[],"yAxisScale":"linear","yAxisMaximumValue":null,"yAxisMinimumValue":null,"columns":[],"label":"","id":"-1"}},"yColumns":null,"seriesColumns":null,"selectedDataOnLoad":{"all":true,"limit":10},"dataPointsTooltip":{"all":false,"limit":1}}},{"id":"b18b9b23-1315-4d7a-ab30-86b9bc0f86e8","title":"built-in ML","visualType":"markdownCard","pageId":"3e0ed903-ea87-40ba-850e-5429d9f555c7","layout":{"x":0,"y":0,"width":24,"height":5},"markdownText":"1. `autocluster` finds common patterns of discrete attributes (dimensions) in the data. It then reduces the results of the original query, whether it's 100 or 100,000 rows, to a few patterns. Based on the Seed-Expand algorithm paper: [Algorithms for Telemetry Data Mining using Discrete Attributes](https://www.scitepress.org/DigitalLibrary/PublicationsDetail.aspx?ID=d5kcrO+cpEU=&t=1)\n\n2. `basket` finds frequent patterns of attributes in the data and returns the patterns that pass a frequency threshold in that data.\n\n3. `diffpatterns` compares two datasets of the same structure and finds patterns of discrete attributes (dimensions) that characterize differences between the two datasets. The plugin is invoked with the evaluate operator. It was developed to help analyze failures (for example, by comparing failures to non-failures in a given time frame). Aims to find significant patterns (that capture portions of the data difference between the sets) and isn't meant for row-by-row differences.","visualOptions":{}}],"baseQueries":[{"id":"1f86430c-e8ca-461e-8a38-cbcc10da4a1e","queryId":"7d36b9f4-5275-4197-8c91-917a0b8ef822","variableName":"results"},{"id":"eeb30253-748d-43d5-b2fb-b8efaa818b2a","queryId":"5a1d3cc8-1b56-4068-990a-2d22913e4f09","variableName":"clustering"}],"parameters":[{"kind":"duration","id":"4c16d048-66f6-45c3-9279-871fb644bf17","displayName":"Time range","description":"","beginVariableName":"_startTime","endVariableName":"_endTime","defaultValue":{"kind":"fixed","start":1451669880000,"end":1695148680150},"showOnPages":{"kind":"all"}},{"kind":"string","id":"82884001-771d-4669-8df3-d6eb81fa435c","displayName":"Forecast Horizon","description":"","variableName":"horizon","selectionType":"scalar","includeAllOption":false,"defaultValue":{"kind":"value","value":"7d"},"dataSource":{"kind":"static","values":[{"value":"3d"},{"value":"7d"},{"value":"30d"},{"value":"365d"}]},"showOnPages":{"kind":"selection","pageIds":["c7acfad2-ddc1-4efc-9f63-6b78be988a84"]}}],"dataSources":[{"id":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2","name":"ML","scopeId":"kusto","clusterUri":"https://demo11.westus.kusto.windows.net/","database":"ML","kind":"manual-kusto"},{"id":"c118a665-bace-48b7-8066-a426b331eb60","name":"7fdf61e2-06d8-4474-a7d5-bcbb585700cc","scopeId":"kusto","clusterUri":"https://trd-rjwm9jc98jph5mdjqy.z6.kusto.data.microsoft.com/","database":"7fdf61e2-06d8-4474-a7d5-bcbb585700cc","kind":"manual-kusto"}],"pages":[{"name":"Anomalies/Forecast","id":"c7acfad2-ddc1-4efc-9f63-6b78be988a84"},{"name":"Needle in Haystack","id":"3e0ed903-ea87-40ba-850e-5429d9f555c7"}],"queries":[{"dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2"},"text":"results\n| summarize EventCount=count(),MinDate=min( TimeStamp), MaxDate=max(TimeStamp)\n\n","id":"13329a64-aa33-42bd-8809-77f370059b07","usedVariables":["results"]},{"dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2"},"text":"let dt=1h;\nresults\n| make-series Cardinality=count() on TimeStamp step dt by OsVer\n| extend Seasons=series_periods_detect(Cardinality, 0, 30d/1h,2)\n| extend Season1=Seasons[0]*(dt/1d)\n| extend Season2=Seasons[1]*(dt/1d)\n| project OsVer, Season1, Season2\n","id":"4317a684-b0ef-4712-bbe0-dff28caf12f5","usedVariables":["results"]},{"dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2"},"text":"results\n| make-series Cardinality=count() on TimeStamp step 1h by OsVer\n| extend Stats = series_stats_dynamic(Cardinality)\n| project OsVer, Min=Stats.min, Max=Stats.max, Avg=Stats.avg, Stats\n","id":"50192d97-86dd-4d01-9bff-080204283896","usedVariables":["results"]},{"dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2"},"text":"results\n| summarize count() by bin(TimeStamp, 1h), OsVer\n","id":"2ff21970-c903-4e0d-a700-a51b6ac02116","usedVariables":["results"]},{"dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2"},"text":"results\n| make-series Cardinality=count() on TimeStamp step 1h by OsVer\n| extend (anomalies, score, baseline) = series_decompose_anomalies(Cardinality) \n","id":"027e24d1-bf09-458f-9bcf-0a35c5ac825e","usedVariables":["results"]},{"dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2"},"text":"let start = toscalar(results | summarize min(TimeStamp));\nlet end = toscalar(results | summarize max(TimeStamp));\nlet dt = 1h;\nresults\n| make-series Cardinality=count() on TimeStamp from start to end+totimespan(horizon) step dt by OsVer\n| extend Forecast = series_decompose_forecast(Cardinality, toint(totimespan(horizon)/dt))\n","id":"3774492b-5f40-452a-a772-21462f4e2fd5","usedVariables":["horizon","results"]},{"dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2"},"text":"clustering\n| make-series Cardinality=count() on PreciseTimeStamp step 10m\n","id":"608b6800-2d3d-42e9-9afe-02837f1ce5f7","usedVariables":["clustering"]},{"dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2"},"text":"let Anchor = datetime(2016-08-23 15:00:00);\nlet WindowWidth=2m;\ndemo_clustering1\n| where PreciseTimeStamp between (_startTime .. _endTime)\n| evaluate autocluster()\n| project Count, Percent, Region, ScaleUnit, DeploymentId, ServiceHost\n","id":"814b380f-a238-4912-9659-c0a6f04886ba","usedVariables":["_endTime","_startTime"]},{"dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2"},"text":"let Anchor = _startTime;\nlet WindowWidth=2m;\ndemo_clustering1\n| where PreciseTimeStamp between ((Anchor-WindowWidth) .. (2*WindowWidth)) or PreciseTimeStamp between ((Anchor-10m) .. (WindowWidth))\n| extend Discriminator = iif(PreciseTimeStamp < Anchor, 'Baseline', 'Anomaly')\n| evaluate diffpatterns(Discriminator, 'Anomaly','Baseline')\n| project PercentA, PercentB, PercentDiffAB, Region, ScaleUnit, DeploymentId, ServiceHost\n","id":"6fbd2d39-4042-4afd-a103-1618672378d3","usedVariables":["_startTime"]},{"dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"c118a665-bace-48b7-8066-a426b331eb60"},"text":"iphone_raw\r\n| project-away applicationId, enrichments, messageProperties, messageSource, templateId, schema\r\n| where  component =='sensors'\r\n| extend telemetry.barometer, telemetry.gyroscope, telemetry.accelerometer, telemetry.magnetometer, toint(telemetry.battery), telemetry.geolocation\r\n| extend telemetry_geolocation.alt, telemetry_geolocation.lat, telemetry_geolocation.lon\r\n| project-away telemetry\r\n| where isnotempty(telemetry_geolocation_lon) and isnotempty(telemetry_geolocation_lat)\r\n| where enqueuedTime >=ago(2m)\r\n| project toreal(telemetry_geolocation_lon), toreal(telemetry_geolocation_lat)\r\n//| getschema \r\n| render scatterchart with (kind=map)\r\n\r\n","id":"e022dd0a-89f5-4f2d-ac3e-7e1fe09f110a","usedVariables":[]},{"dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"c118a665-bace-48b7-8066-a426b331eb60"},"text":"iphone_raw\n| where enqueuedTime > ago(1h)\n| where  component =='sensors'\n| extend toint(telemetry.battery)\n| summarize max(telemetry_battery) by enqueuedTime\n//| getschema \n| render areachart  \n\n","id":"c6503722-6a84-43a6-b53b-2c56b6fb3e11","usedVariables":[]},{"id":"7d36b9f4-5275-4197-8c91-917a0b8ef822","dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2"},"text":"demo_make_series1\n| where TimeStamp between (['_startTime'] .. ['_endTime'])","usedVariables":["_endTime","_startTime"]},{"id":"5a1d3cc8-1b56-4068-990a-2d22913e4f09","dataSource":{"kind":"inline","dataSourceId":"18dbf745-2403-4761-a2ea-c25ddc7e6de2"},"text":"demo_clustering1\n| where PreciseTimeStamp between (['_startTime'] .. ['_endTime'])","usedVariables":["_endTime","_startTime"]}]}